    "text": "To determine how much Scott, Mary, and Ken have exceeded their goal, we need to calculate the amount each person has raised and then sum these amounts. Let's start with the information given:\n\n1. Ken has $600.\n2. Mary's collection is five times what Ken has.\n3. Mary's collection is also three times Scott's funds.\n\nFirst, we calculate Mary's collection:\n\\[ \\text{Mary's collection} = 5 \\times \\text{Ken's collection} = 5 \\times 600 = 3000 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate Scott's collection:\n\\[ \\text{Scott's collection} = \\frac{\\text{Mary's collection}}{3} = \\frac{3000}{3} = 1000 \\]\n\nNow, we sum the amounts raised by Scott, Mary, and Ken:\n\\[ \\text{Total amount raised} = \\text{Scott's collection} + \\text{Mary's collection} + \\text{Ken's collection} = 1000 + 3000 + 600 = 4600 \\]\n\nThe goal was to raise $4000, so we need to find out how much they have exceeded their goal:\n\\[ \\text{Amount exceeded} = \\text{Total amount raised} - \\text{Goal} = 4600 - 4000 = 600 \\]\n\nTherefore, the three have exceeded their goal by \\(\\boxed{600}\\).",
